      "id": "GLTF-241",
      "summary": "A primitive with COLOR_0 and a metallic-roughness material cannot be imported as the file asks, and the loss runs one layer deeper than the material: the stride-24 layout a coloured primitive lands on has no Normal slot either, so an authored NORMAL is discarded and the primitive cannot be lit at all. Supporting the combination means a new stride plus a shader variant on every renderer, the same blast radius that ruled out colour-space option A. GLTF-241's acceptance allows the other outcome -- REPORTED, not silently downgraded -- and that is what landed: MeshOut names both losses and both loaders log them.",
